From 3e4c7d89199d9b6389dfdfb25cf3d81fabfe0b6e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lucas Santos <lsantos7654@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 20 Apr 2026 21:22:13 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 04/21] Non-destructive agent reload endpoint
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds `POST /global/reload-agents` to opencode that re-reads agents/*.md
for every active instance without disposing the InstanceState. Unlike
`POST /global/dispose`, this does NOT SIGTERM MCP subprocesses, so an
in-flight tool call (the hivemind MCP server itself, when called via
the MCP transport) survives the reload.

Hivemind switches `notify_instance_reload` from /global/dispose to
this endpoint after `enable_agent` / `disable_agent` mutations, so the
user no longer has to type `continue` after every catalog change.

Mechanism:
  - Adds Config.invalidateState() Effect — a non-destructive variant
    of Config.invalidate() that just clears the per-instance Config
    InstanceState cache (no Instance.disposeAll).
  - Adds Agent.reload() Effect — chains Config.invalidateState() with
    Agent's own InstanceState invalidation, then publishes a new
    Agent.AgentsChanged Bus event so subscribers (TUI, etc.) can
    refresh.
  - Adds Agent.reloadAll() static — iterates Instance.directories()
    and runs reload() in each context.
  - Adds Instance.directories() — exposes the cached instance keys so
    Agent.reloadAll can iterate them without breaking encapsulation.
  - Adds POST /global/reload-agents route that calls Agent.reloadAll()
    and emits a new AgentsReloadedEvent on GlobalBus.
